From: brkosebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: NCM retry after busy aggregation flush

Retry timer-driven aggregation flush after TX request exhaustion at the next bounded timer interval.

Integration fixups are folded into the final delta. Device observations apply
to the integration build; the isolated topic requires qualification.

Assisted-by: LLM
---

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
index bf02545b3..70a0f8952 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
@@ -1158,7 +1158,11 @@ static enum hrtimer_restart ncm_tx_timeout(struct hrtimer *data)
 		 *
 		 * This will call directly into u_ether's eth_start_xmit()
 		 */
-		netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev);
+		if (netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev) == NETDEV_TX_BUSY) {
+			/* No request was available; the partial NTB still needs a flush. */
+			hrtimer_forward_now(data, TX_TIMEOUT_NSECS);
+			return HRTIMER_RESTART;
+		}
 	}
 	return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 }
